`260-270`: _🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**The timeout branch pops `completed` without the single-driver check.**

The header now promises a panic when a driver-only entry point runs while a select is parked. This branch skips `checkSingleDriverLocked()` and pops a completion anyway. A `timedWait` that times out while another task's select holds `reg` steals the completion silently, which is the failure mode the claim protocol removes elsewhere.

The same applies to two other consuming sections: `cancel`'s wait loop at Lines 521-523 unlinks from `completed`, and `drainPending` at Lines 604-611 drops completions on `.discard`. `cancelAll` covers the latter through `requestCancelAll`, but only on the first pass; a select registering mid-drain is not caught.


🩹 Add the check to the timeout branch

```diff
                 error.Timeout => {
                     // A completion, or the close, can still have landed
                     // together with the timeout; report those rather than a
                     // timeout that did not happen.
                     self.mutex.lock();
+                    self.checkSingleDriverLocked();
                     const n = self.completed.pop();
```



