F12.body:
`1660-1678`: _🚀 Performance & Scalability_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _💤 Low value_

**The quiescence watch burns a lot of CI time for a probabilistic signal.**

200 rounds × 500 passes × `@sizeOf(CompletionQueue)` bytes is on the order of ten million `expectEqual` calls, each spawning 4 tasks and 64 timers beforehand. The comment already states the honest position: at the real gap width a pass is one more clean sample, not proof. That is fine as a test, but the current constants pay full price for it on every run.

Consider dropping the inner watch to a smaller count, or comparing with `std.mem.allEqual` so the hot loop is one call instead of one per byte.


♻️ Cheaper inner watch

```diff
         `@memset`(std.mem.asBytes(&cq), 0xAA);
         var checks: u32 = 0;
-        while (checks < 500) : (checks += 1) {
-            for (std.mem.asBytes(&cq)) |b| {
-                try std.testing.expectEqual(0xAA, b);
-            }
+        while (checks < 50) : (checks += 1) {
+            try std.testing.expect(std.mem.allEqual(u8, std.mem.asBytes(&cq), 0xAA));
         }
```



